Keep the app from shifting sideways when the closed workspace rail gets focus.

Since v0.16 the closed workspace rail stays mounted, parked 12px past the
window's right edge (translateX in index.css). AppShell passes it
inert={!workspacePanelVisible}, but React 18 drops a boolean inert prop, so
its 14 controls stayed in the Tab order. Tabbing into one, or anything else
scrolling it into view, scrolled the body 12px (18px at a larger zoom) and
the whole app, sidebar included, stayed shifted left until a reload. The rail
now sets the attribute on its node, as ExecutionLogsPanel does, and
.app-shell clips its horizontal overflow so nothing can scroll it sideways.
Upstream fix to backport; delete this patch once upstream ships one.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0025-codex-bypass-default.patch.
diff --git a/web/src/index.css b/web/src/index.css
index 338b9ee0f..82f66f504 100644
--- a/web/src/index.css
+++ b/web/src/index.css
@@ -620,6 +620,14 @@
   }
 }
 
+/* Nothing may scroll the app sideways. The closed workspace rail sits 12px
+   past the right edge (translateX above), and anything scrolled into view
+   there shifted the whole app, sidebar included, to the left. `clip`, unlike
+   `hidden`, can't be scrolled by script or focus. */
+.app-shell {
+  overflow-x: clip;
+}
+
 /* The transparent <main> shows the palette canvas through. */
 .app-shell {
   background: var(--background);
